    "title": "Cyber-शिक्षित 2.0",
    "description": "Cyber-शिक्षित 2.0 – Your Internet, Your Safety is a four-day outreach initiative organized by the IEEE Women in Engineering (WIE) Pulchowk Affinity Group for students of Grades 8, 9, and 10 in six secondary and high schools in Tanahun District. The program focuses on improving students’ digital literacy and cybersecurity awareness and helping them become safer and more responsible users of technology. Through interactive sessions, students will learn about online privacy, password security, safe account practices, cyberbullying, digital consent, safe online interactions, and financial security. We aim to reach at least 40% female population out of 500 targeted students. The program builds upon the success of the previous Cyber-शिक्षित outreach program, which reached more than 250 secondary students across five public schools in Kavre District. Through Cyber-शिक्षित 2.0, IEEE WIE Pulchowk aims to promote safe online behavior, strengthen cybersecurity awareness, and expand equitable access to digital education in communities beyond Kathmandu. Event Highlights Inspiring Talks: Women in tech and STEM career opportunities. Digital Literacy: Safe, responsible, and confident use of technology. Cybersecurity Awareness: Privacy, passwords, accounts, and online safety. Interactive Demos: Explore AI and digital technologies. Hands-on Learning: Quizzes, activities, and real-life scenarios Fun & Engagement: Games, Q&A, teamwork, and prizes.",
