    "id": "578393",
    "title": "Data-Thon 2026",
    "description": "Data-Thon 2026: Data-Driven Innovation for Business and Society is an interdisciplinary, hands-on student innovation event organized by the IEEE TEMS Student Branch Chapter at BNM Institute of Technology (BNMIT), Bengaluru. The Data-Thon will provide students with an opportunity to apply data analytics, artificial intelligence, Generative AI, data visualization tools like Power BI, Tableau, Excel and Python, design thinking and technology-management concepts to real-world business and societal challenges. Participants will work in interdisciplinary teams to understand a problem, identify relevant data, generate insights and develop a feasible technology-enabled solution. The event will include a preparatory orientation, expert sessions, problem-solving activities, mentoring and a final solution presentation. Challenge tracks will cover areas such as AI for Business, Smart Operations, FinTech, Sustainability and Social Innovation. Industry professionals and faculty members will mentor and evaluate teams, helping students connect technical solutions with business value, feasibility and societal impact. The activity aims to strengthen student’s data literacy, technology-management capabilities, innovation skills, teamwork, communication and entrepreneurial thinking. The event is expected to engage approximately 150–200 students and generate multiple data-driven prototypes or solution concepts. The outcomes will be documented through student projects, presentations, photographs, feedback and an impact report to support future TEMS activities and establish the Data-Thon as a recurring annual chapter initiative.",
