    "id": "581586",
    "title": "WIE UNAJ Social Innovation Hackathon",
    "description": "The IEEE Women in Engineering Affinity Group of the Universidad Nacional de Juliaca (WIE UNAJ), in collaboration with the IEEE UNAJ Student Branch, will organize a one-day, in-person hackathon focused on developing innovative solutions to a social problem affecting the city of Juliaca. The event will bring together university students from different academic backgrounds who will be randomly assigned to multidisciplinary teams at the beginning of the activity. Each team will analyze the proposed local challenge, identify its main causes and needs, and develop a creative and feasible project to address it. Throughout the day, participants will work collaboratively through different stages, including problem analysis, ideation, solution development, prototyping, and final presentation. The activity will encourage students to apply their technical knowledge while strengthening teamwork, leadership, creativity, communication, and problem-solving skills. WIE UNAJ will promote an inclusive environment that encourages the active participation and leadership of women in STEM. Participants will receive guidance and support from organizers, mentors, and members of the IEEE community during the development of their projects. The event will be held entirely in person at the Universidad Nacional de Juliaca – Capilla, and lunch will be provided to participants as part of the full-day activity. At the end of the hackathon, each team will present its proposed solution to a jury, with projects evaluated according to criteria such as innovation, social impact, feasibility, and quality of the proposed solution.",
