    "title": "CyberShield: Student Workshop on Cybersecurity Essentials and Digital Safety",
    "description": "This hands-on workshop brings college students together to build essential skills in cybersecurity and digital safety. As technology becomes increasingly central to daily life, knowing how to write secure code, spot online threats, and protect data is crucial for future technical leaders. Led by experienced cybersecurity professionals, the interactive sessions will provide participants with real-world technical strategies and industry insights. Attendees will engage in practical threat-detection scenarios and learn actionable methods for securing personal and organizational systems. By offering hands-on training in a specialized field, the workshop directly supports IEEE WIE's mission to foster technological excellence and encourage student interest in STEM disciplines. Beyond the technical training, the event creates a collaborative space for students to network, seek guidance, and build confidence in pursuing security careers. Educating the student community on digital safety aligns directly with IEEE's broader vision of advancing technology for the benefit of humanity. Through interactive learning and skill-building, the program helps bridge the technical knowledge gap for emerging engineers and computer scientists. Ultimately, students will walk away with practical competencies, valuable peer connections, and a stronger foundation to navigate and secure today's digital landscape.",
