    "id": "582968",
    "title": "IEEE Robotics Workshop 2026",
    "description": "IEEE Robotics Workshop 2026 – Robotics, Automation & Obstacle Avoiding Robot IEEE Student Branch HBTU-K, IEEE Power Electronics Society Student Branch Chapter HBTU-K, and IEEE Women in Engineering Student Branch Affinity Group HBTU-K present IEEE Robotics Workshop 2026 , an interactive and hands-on technical workshop focused on Robotics, Automation, Embedded Systems and Robotic Control . The workshop is designed to provide students with practical exposure to the fundamentals of robotics and automation while enabling them to understand how sensors, motors, electronic circuits, microcontrollers and programming work together to build a functional robotic system. As part of the workshop, participants will work on an Obstacle Avoiding Robot , gaining hands-on experience in programming, sensor integration, motor control, hardware interfacing, testing and troubleshooting. Workshop Highlights 🤖 Introduction to Robotics & Automation ⚙️ Motors & Robotic Mechanisms 🔌 Circuits, Sensors & Hardware Integration 💻 Programming & Robotic Control 📡 Ultrasonic Sensor & Obstacle Detection 🔧 Motor Control using L298N 🛠️ Hands-on Obstacle Avoiding Robot 🔬 Build, Test & Troubleshoot Your Robot 📜 Certificate of Participation The workshop will encourage participants to move beyond theoretical learning and develop practical problem-solving, programming, hardware integration and teamwork skills through a real-world robotics project.",
