    "description": "IEEE Day 2026 is proposed to be celebrated by the IEEE SIRCRRCOE Student Branch on 12th and 13th October 2026 under the theme “Leveraging Technology for a Better Tomorrow.” The event aims to create awareness about IEEE, its activities, technical opportunities, and the importance of technological advancements among students. The first day will feature technical events under SPS, SC, PES, and CS, along with the IEEE Xtreme 20.0 poster release and promotional activities to encourage student participation. The second day will include an inauguration ceremony, a cultural performance, a presentation on the journey of the IEEE SIRCRRCOE Student Branch, addresses by college authorities and faculty advisors, guest felicitation, and a keynote session. Non-technical activities such as Make a Reel and Rapid Fire are also planned. E-certificates will be provided to participants, while winners may receive gifts or physical certificates. The celebration aims to promote IEEE membership, innovation, technical learning, creativity, collaboration, and awareness of IEEE's role in empowering students for a better tomorrow.",
