    "id": "582661",
    "title": "IEEEXtreme Collaboration On-site Event - Third Meet",
    "description": "Overall: Officers from both IEEE ISET Bizerte Student Branch and IEEE FSB Student Branch met to discuss the organization and coordination of the IEEE Xtreme event and accompanying bootcamp, including logistics, session structure, speaker planning, task distribution, and follow-up preparations. Discussion points : 1. Event Planning and Administrative Coordination The overall planning of the IEEE Xtreme event was discussed, including coordination with the administration and confirmation of the event arrangements. The teams also discussed the possibility of organizing the event at FSB. 2. Registration and Promotional Posts The registration process and promotional communication were discussed, including the preparation of registration forms and posts for the bootcamp. The responsibilities for preparing and publishing the content were also reviewed. 3. Bootcamp Structure and Session Planning Different approaches for structuring the bootcamp were discussed, including an introductory session followed by several technical sessions. The possibility of organizing sessions progressively over several weeks was also considered. 4. Introduction to IEEE Xtreme and Competitive Programming An introductory session covering IEEE Xtreme and competitive programming was proposed to help participants understand the competition, its format, and the fundamentals before moving to more advanced topics. 5. Technical and Non-Technical Sessions The team discussed combining technical sessions with non-technical topics such as stress and time management. The sessions would be organized progressively, with technical topics forming the core of the bootcamp. 6. Speakers and Session Topics Potential speakers and topics were discussed, including Data Structures, Algorithms, STL, and Binary Search. Speakers were encouraged to suggest topics based on their expertise and experience. 7. Session Scheduling and Coordination The team discussed scheduling sessions at regular intervals and coordinating with speakers to confirm their availability and assigned topics. The aim was to maintain a consistent and organized progression throughout the bootcamp. 8. Follow-Up and Communication The importance of maintaining communication between the teams and following up with speakers was emphasized. Updates and confirmations would be shared among the organizers to ensure smooth preparation and coordination.",
