    "description": "UIT University organized IEEEXtreme Awareness Session 2 , led by Proctor Ambassador Syeda Aimen Naseem , Assistant Professor and Student Branch Chair at UIT University. The session was organized to familiarize students with IEEEXtreme , the global 24-hour programming competition organized by IEEE, and to encourage students to explore opportunities for participation, collaboration, and competitive programming. The session provided students with an overview of the IEEEXtreme competition format, eligibility, team formation, registration process, and participation requirements . Students were also introduced to the nature of programming challenges featured in the competition and the importance of problem-solving, logical thinking, algorithmic skills, and effective teamwork in achieving success in a competitive environment. The session further emphasized the academic and professional benefits of participating in IEEEXtreme , including strengthening programming capabilities, gaining exposure to an international technical community, and developing confidence through competition. Through her guidance and motivation, Syeda Aimen Naseem encouraged students to actively participate and represent UIT University on the international stage , contributing to a stronger culture of technical learning and innovation within the university.",
