    "id": "579873",
    "title": "IEEEXtreme Awareness Session 1",
    "description": "IEEEXtreme is an international programming competition organized by IEEE, designed to challenge students to solve complex computational problems through teamwork, creativity, and efficient programming. The awareness session will introduce students to the competition, its objectives, participation process, eligibility criteria, and the benefits of taking part in this global platform. The session will provide an overview of the competition format, including team formation, registration, preparation strategies, problem-solving techniques, and the overall competition experience. Participants will also learn about the skills that can be developed through IEEEXtreme, including algorithmic thinking, coding proficiency, time management, teamwork, and logical reasoning. The session will also feature guidance for students who are interested in participating for the first time. Experienced participants or organizers may share preparation tips, useful resources, common challenges, and practical recommendations for improving competitive programming skills. The goal is to motivate students to explore competitive programming and encourage greater participation in IEEEXtreme.",
