    "title": "Sponsorship Memorandum Signing for IEEEXtreme 20.0",
    "description": "The IEEE Student Branch at the Islamic University of Gaza announced the signing of a sponsorship memorandum between the Islamic University of Gaza and Medad Al-Khair Campaign for Urgent Relief to support the participation of students from the Gaza Strip in the 20th edition of the global IEEEXtreme programming competition. The memorandum was signed on behalf of the Islamic University of Gaza by Prof. Ammar Mohammad Abu Hadrous , Dean of Scientific Research and Graduate Studies, and on behalf of Medad Al-Khair Campaign for Urgent Relief by Mr. Hammam Hamdan Abu Rouk , with coordination by Eng. Hamada Raja Abu Rujaila , Supervisor of the IEEE Student Branch at the Islamic University of Gaza. The sponsorship aims to support the participation of 40 student teams, representing 120 students, and facilitate their participation in the 24-hour global programming competition. The Islamic University of Gaza will host the competition, while the IEEE Student Branch will oversee the organization, implementation, and technical and administrative coordination of the event. This initiative reflects a commitment to empowering students, supporting their technical development, and providing them with opportunities to participate in international academic and programming competitions.",
