    "id": "558175",
    "title": "Tomorrow Land 3.0:CS Benefits",
    "description": "Speaker: Molka Wesleti Date: April 18th, 2026 Session Purpose & Chapter Impact: Objective of the Session and How it aligns with chapter goals: The primary objective of this session was to provide a strategic roadmap for students to navigate the vast ecosystem of the IEEE Computer Society . By focusing on high-impact competitions and leadership tracks, the session aligns with the IEEE CS ENSIT Student Branch Chapter ’s mission to foster technical excellence and competitive spirit. It aimed to bridge the gap between simple membership and active participation in global initiatives, ensuring that members are equipped to represent the chapter at both national and international levels. Session Content & Outcomes: Overview: Brief description of the session: Titled \"CS Benefits\" ,this session was a cornerstone of Tomorrow Land 3.0 Day 1. Led by Molka Wesleti, former Vice Chair of IEEE CS ENSIT , the workshop served as a masterclass in leveraging IEEE resources. It moved beyond the basics to showcase how technical challenges and student initiatives can define an engineering student’s professional trajectory. Key Topics Covered: IEEE CS TSYP Technical Challenge: A detailed guide on the Tunisia Students and Young Professionals (TSYP) Congress, focusing on the Computer Society's specific technical track, preparation strategies, and the importance of national networking. IEEEXtreme: An in-depth look at the prestigious 24-hour global programming competition, covering everything from the registration mechanics to the mental and technical stamina required for success. IEEE CS SYP Initiatives: An exploration of the Student and Young Professional programs, highlighting opportunities for international volunteering, leadership roles, and the global Career Center. Activities Conducted: Comprehensive Presentation: A visual breakdown of competition timelines, technical prerequisites, and the ranking systems for TSYP and IEEEXtreme . Mentorship & Strategic Advice: The speaker shared practical insights on team composition, how to select complementary skill sets for coding challenges, and effective time management during high-pressure events. Interactive Q&A Session: A dynamic dialogue where participants addressed specific concerns regarding the learning curve for IEEEXtreme and how to get involved in SYP activities as a newcomer. Learning Outcomes: Key skills and knowledge gained: Participants acquired a clear understanding of the \"IEEE CS Path.\" They learned how to strategically prepare for national technical challenges (TSYP) and global coding marathons (IEEEXtreme). Furthermore, they gained knowledge on how to utilize SYP initiatives to build a professional network that extends beyond their university years, understanding that IEEE CS is a gateway to international industry recognition. Participant Engagement: Interaction level: High. Notable participation highlights: The session saw exceptional engagement, particularly when discussing the TSYP Technical Challenge. Many students expressed a direct interest in forming study groups for IEEEXtreme , demonstrating that the session successfully transitioned from passive listening to active community building. Conclusion & Evaluation: Overall Evaluation: The session was an overwhelming success and acted as a vital motivational catalyst for Tomorrow Land 3.0 . Molka Wesleti’s expertise as a former leader provided the \"insider perspective\" that resonated deeply with the audience. By demystifying the CS benefits and focusing on actionable goals like IEEEXtreme and TSYP , the workshop left the participants empowered, informed, and ready to take on the technical challenges of the upcoming hackathon and beyond.",
