    "title": "CS TAM Booth at the Heart of IEEEXtreme19.0",
    "description": "During the IEEEXtreme 19.0 event held at ISIMM , the IEEE Computer Society (CS) Chapter organized a CS TAM 2.0 promotional booth led by Wassim Gasmi , the CS TAM 2.0 Ambassador . This initiative aimed to introduce participants to the Computer Society Tunisia Annual Meeting (CS TAM) and highlight the opportunities it offers for learning, networking, and professional development within the IEEE community. Objectives Promote the CS TAM 2.0 event among IEEEXtreme participants. Encourage new memberships and increase awareness of the Computer Society’s role and benefits. Strengthen community engagement and motivate participants to take part in upcoming CS initiatives . Activities and Outcomes The booth was set up at the center of the IEEEXtreme venue , attracting considerable attention from competitors and visitors. Participants had the opportunity to learn about the CS TAM 2.0 program , its technical sessions , and networking opportunities . A large number of students registered on-site, showing enthusiasm about joining the Computer Society and being part of future events. The initiative received positive feedback , reflecting strong interest in the Computer Society’s vision and the excitement surrounding the upcoming congress. Conclusion The CS TAM 2.0 booth , organized by Wassim Gasmi , successfully achieved its objectives by engaging participants, promoting the Computer Society, and strengthening IEEE ISIMM SB’s visibility within the IEEEXtreme environment. The event demonstrated the value of combining technical competition with community promotion , and it set a positive tone for further involvement in CS TAM 2.0 and related IEEE initiatives.",
