    "title": "XTREME 19.0",
    "description": "IEEE XTREME 19.0 is a 24-hour global competitive programming contest organized annually by the Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE). The event challenges participants to solve a series of algorithmic and real-world problem statements using their programming and analytical skills within a limited timeframe. Teams compete at a global level, emphasizing accuracy, efficiency, and teamwork. The Raghu IEEE Student Branch hosted IEEE XTREME 19.0 with active participation from students across various departments. Prior to the event, awareness sessions and orientation programs were conducted to familiarize participants with the contest format, rules, and coding platforms. Registered teams participated under the guidance of IEEE-assigned proctors, ensuring adherence to IEEE guidelines and maintaining the integrity of the competition. During the contest, participants worked continuously for 24 hours, collaboratively analyzing problems, designing optimized solutions, and implementing them using appropriate programming languages. The event environment promoted focus, time management, and collaborative learning. Continuous monitoring and technical support were provided throughout the competition to ensure smooth conduct. IEEE XTREME 19.0 provided students with exposure to global competitive standards, enhanced their problem-solving abilities, and encouraged innovation and perseverance. The successful organization of the event by Raghu IEEE Student Branch strengthened technical culture on campus and motivated students to actively engage in future IEEE activities.",
